+4. Press F8 to turn combat on, heal low HP, and maintain prepared buffs even with no enemy selected. Repeated F8 presses leave it on. It checks for the enemy you select, fights it, then waits for your next selection after the kill. F9 turns combat off. F7 is a single on/off toggle (on like F8, off like F9) for controllers that map a button to F7; the helper consumes F7 so EQ's own Target Nearest PC does not also fire. F8 assist never selects or moves. F11 starts/stops a stationary one-kill camp test with automatic target selection; F8 switches back to assist. F12 recording stays disabled. You control melee yourself; F9 stops further helper input but does not turn melee off or cancel a spell already cast.
 5. At full health, click Find / calibrate HP, check the proposed inner red gauge, and Save only when that outline and full HP are correct. Drag a corrected rectangle if needed. Automatic healing requires this reading. F10 requests your fast heal even without calibration.
 6. Optional: calibrate the blue mana bar. Below 25% mana the assistant saves mana for healing; at 35% or less it also skips buffs, stuns and the Smite ability.

